{"title":"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Characteristic_Polynomials)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Characteristic Polynomials)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84a63b2ce6df9669ae649aad2636f15f17c3974a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_n=\\tfrac{1}{2}(a^n+b^n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />  where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873e474b4f90e2ca4f1f60faca959c407c4f6dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3+2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b66ac85cf6c851ae61680390b47b6e2ab99c1bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3-2\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296b43d54f6970fedbe38c198b1106d6d24b0676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0,1,2,\\cdots,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be09ffa290a58d370b8cf5970cf83c308cb874ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{12345}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> is an integer.  Its units digit is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3f1083034c4d409fadfde193712f24d88b1b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 1\\quad \\text{(B) } 3\\quad \\text{(C) } 5\\quad \\text{(D) } 7\\quad \\text{(E) } 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/564360ee8243872bedae4fd3ca2d02d633245b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)R_n=\\tfrac12(a^{n+1}+b^{n+1})+ab\\cdot\\tfrac12(a^{n-1}+b^{n-1})=R_{n+1}+abR_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"528\" height=\"21\" />\nbut <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/35140077cead97e919bd1475a7d132f6da542123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2fbad6d76459307b6f377b0007124f3c48e47a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, so this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab68a7fcd0a483080794ff2b7076463f86bc7f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{n+1}=6R_n-R_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf732922cf1bdd78606f94ff6e3ddf23ffac1e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/0/830d50003897c865d7d5c107fd13371f00066c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, all terms are integers and we can continue the recurrence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d00d19218c2ab4b9906de0e0445deb3b6b2d5b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rm{mod}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> to get the repeating sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/9620a5e4547115df9fa2aa215e4d695cbab54e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3,7,9,7,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/70721c830aa84eadb8417a0352d5ae02ead8d5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by three but not by six, so the required element in the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62effaf0d5dc9bfa1d137bed40c4baa73698962d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Characteristic_Polynomials.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Characteristic_Polynomials)\">Solution 2 (Characteristic Polynomials)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Characteristic Polynomials)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/891cd277a7bdcae35048c01ce97b5432531cc1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\pm 2\\sqrt{2} = 3 \\pm \\sqrt{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"21\" /> must be the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b78b0f6299fe2acde56b0271e4ae1e340d6e4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 3)^2 - 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/92662271134d223eaadabf6d01b937a187f4d42b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 6x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />.  So the characteristic polynomial of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad9877ac72b883c33c44bf668e87120937d8f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{R_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/92662271134d223eaadabf6d01b937a187f4d42b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 6x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, and thus the recurrence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d0255583c7cd86a8864539a7d4e05044ca8e1f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_n = 6R_{n-1} - R_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" /> holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb34c8e5b7bf4d51b586190d6321bc5c6b8776d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a8daf9b55d101081de5ca6ead113b19adf55dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fb734096ba7000d06944c083ecf0914ecffef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> is an integer for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> be the last digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fb734096ba7000d06944c083ecf0914ecffef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />.  Using the recurrence relation, the first terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/5906e8737026ada076032fba69da6f4d2e8550e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{S_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/118ce7640600371cfe85d6d7b284bfd97d2bc2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2652c18683d93705b6e82246a328d917b04f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 3, 7, 9, 7, 3, 1, 3, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"17\" />  \n</p><p>Since each term of this sequence depends solely on the previous two terms, this sequence cycles every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms.  The remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/70721c830aa84eadb8417a0352d5ae02ead8d5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78ed7d32e1781b55e6831ca5cb0d60dbdddae1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{12345} = S_3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"167\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d5b948fd2e8a82be18042d192710914b5e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd47a2d4835d421aa7d95e0001e9f09dd7d5530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\right)^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"35\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7ef77fc05f9035adeff4923b80e4dedc25edf08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"23\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integers.  Furthermore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b016faa98129def544b100411e031ed43e4458a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\right)^n = x + y\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"187\" height=\"35\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integers, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8828b501512e913550a94cc686d2c82379bb26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(3 - 2\\sqrt{2}\\right)^n = x - y\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"187\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c2c794324d43d075a8cf011879e5360ca9731eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{y_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> be sequences of integers such that for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d5b948fd2e8a82be18042d192710914b5e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/794f4dbbc569b512c200ab8fa03b9bf43dd158ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\right)^n = x_n + y_n\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"205\" height=\"35\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/e/51ee790e960562b29c96e234931617f2fc6ea940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\right)^{n+1} = \\left(3 + 2\\sqrt{2}\\right)\\left(x_n + y_n\\sqrt{2}\\right) = (3x_n + 4y_n) + (2x_n + 3y_n)\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"586\" height=\"37\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a88844e798d8eca9ebe1259b248202a22e4e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} = 3x_n + 4y_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46021e249d36ff21e534b920291d9e0bf4733b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{n+1} = 2x_n + 3y_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p>The first few ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a56b1526cf38268aae07b6cf67ea94c8d9a55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n, y_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, starting with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3ea5ae5f5092b7024a8775d282032dc76120c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_0, y_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />, are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/2451fb76b8e2ed951c262cfbd77594eeca7394b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 0), (3, 2), (7, 2), (9, 0), (7, 8), (3, 8), (1, 0), ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"356\" height=\"20\" />.  Since each ordered pair in this sequence depends solely on the previous ordered pair, this sequence must cycle every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> entries.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/1915b2d984e093f12e4e2eb89c08e076ef9d39c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_n = \\frac{1}{2}\\left((x_n + y_n \\sqrt{2}) + (x_n - y_n \\sqrt{2})\\right) = x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"348\" height=\"38\" />, the last digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be09ffa290a58d370b8cf5970cf83c308cb874ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{12345}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc340f475ecf68303b67e489351ceb91b5f19079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{12345}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93beae3a438ab1a57db421ea43903e74d1578094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12345 \\equiv 3\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50fedc0a83f7cbdd1bddaec4335ff1d629a47996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{12345} \\equiv x_{3} \\equiv \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9}\\ (\\text{mod}\\ 10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"241\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME\" title=\"1990 AHSME\">1990 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1990 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1990\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problem 30</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1990 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index